Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Break orphan-repair ties by fine index; number the test
 after #893

Equal distances go to the lower fine index, and a query widens while the first
free candidate ties with the last neighbour found, so the claims no longer
depend on how many neighbours were asked for. Development's claims on exact
ties depended on its k = orphans + 8: on half-cell-offset grids the bounded
query without this tie-break already differed from development (104 to 1,472
entries), and no bounded query can reproduce that order.

Still bit-identical to development on every call in the custom-MG and
placed-ribbon tests (98), on K1's #893 fixture at refinement 4 (orphans 10 and
38) and on 40 random 2-D and 3-D clouds.

The memory test moves to test_0893 (test_1015 is taken twice already).

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
